{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-pro-30-1","title":"Proverbs 30:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Agur's confession of his faith. 7 The two points of his prayer. 10 The meanest are not to be wronged. 11 Four wicked generations. 15 Four things insatiable. 17 Parents are not to be despised. 18 Four things hard to be known. 21 Four things intolerable. 24 Four things exceeding wise. 29 Four things stately. 32 Wrath is to be prevented.</p>\n<p>Agur.Agur was probably a public teacher, and Ithiel and Ucal, his pupils; and this was the {massa,} or oracle, which he delivered, not by his own wisdom, but by the Holy Spirit, for the benefit of man; and which, it is probable, was added by \"the men of Hezekiah.\"</p>\n<p>even. 31:1; 2Pe 1:19-21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-2","title":"Proverbs 30:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>I am. Job 42:3-6; Ps 73:22; Isa 6:5; Ro 11:25; 1Co 3:18; 8:2; Jas 1:5 brutish. 5:12; Ps 92:6; Jer 10:14; 2Pe 2:12-16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-3","title":"Proverbs 30:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>neither. Am 7:14,15; Mt 16:17 nor. Job 11:7-9; Mt 11:27; Joh 17:3; Ro 11:33; Eph 3:18,19 have. Heb. know. the holy Isa 6:3,10; 30:11; 57:15; Re 3:7; 4:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-4","title":"Proverbs 30:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Who hath ascended. De 30:12; Joh 3:13; Ro 10:6; Eph 4:9,10 who hath gathered. Job 38:4-41; Ps 104:2-35; Isa 40:12-31; 53:8 what is his name. Ex 3:13-15; 6:3; 34:5-7; De 28:58 and what. Ge 32:29; Jud 13:18; Ps 2:7; Isa 7:14; 9:6; Jer 23:6; Mt 1:21-23 Mt 11:27; Lu 10:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-5","title":"Proverbs 30:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>word. Ps 12:6; 18:30; 19:8; 119:140; Ro 7:12; Jas 3:17 pure. Heb. purified. Ge 15:1; Ps 84:11; 91:2; 115:9-11; 144:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-6","title":"Proverbs 30:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>Add. De 4:2; 12:32; Re 22:18,19 and. Job 13:7-9; 1Co 15:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-7","title":"Proverbs 30:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>have. 1Ki 3:5-9; 2Ki 2:9; Ps 27:4; Lu 10:42 deny me them not. Heb. withhold them not from me. Ps 21:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-8","title":"Proverbs 30:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Remove. 21:6; 22:8; 23:5; Ps 62:9,10; 119:29,37; Ec 1:2; Isa 5:18; 59:4 Joh 2:8; Ac 14:15 feed. Ge 28:20; 48:15,16; Ex 16:15,18,21,22,29,35; Mt 6:11,33; Lu 11:3 1Ti 6:6-8 convenient for me. Heb. of my allowance. 2Ki 25:30; Jer 37:21; 52:34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-9","title":"Proverbs 30:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>I be full. De 6:10-12; 8:10-14; 31:20; 32:15; Ne 9:25,26; Job 31:24-28 Jer 2:31; Eze 16:14,15,49,50; Da 4:17,30; Ho 13:6; Ac 12:22,23 deny thee. Heb. belie thee. Who. Ex 5:2; 2Ch 32:15-17 or. 6:30,31; Ps 125:3 and take the name. 29:24; Ex 20:7; Le 5:1; Mt 26:72,74</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-10","title":"Proverbs 30:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>Accuse not. Heb. Hurt not with thy tongue. 24:23; De 23:15; 1Sa 22:9,10; 24:9; 26:19; 30:15; 2Sa 16:1-4 2Sa 19:26,27; Da 3:8-18; 6:13,24; Ro 14:4 lest. 11:26; 24:24; 28:27; De 15:9; 2Ch 24:22-24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-11","title":"Proverbs 30:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>a generation. 12-14; Mt 3:7; 1Pe 2:9 that curseth. 17; 20:20; Le 20:9; De 21:20,21; 27:16; Mt 15:4-6; Mr 7:10-13 doth. 1Ti 5:4,8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-12","title":"Proverbs 30:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>that are. 21:2; Jud 17:5,13; 1Sa 15:13,14; Job 33:9; Ps 36:2; Isa 65:5 Jer 2:22-24,35; Lu 11:39,40; 16:15; 18:11; 2Ti 3:5; Tit 1:15,16 1Jo 1:8-10 not. Ps 51:2,7; Isa 1:16; Jer 4:14; Eze 36:25; Zec 13:1; 1Co 6:11 Tit 3:5; 1Jo 1:7; Re 1:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-13","title":"Proverbs 30:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>6:17; 21:4; Ps 101:5; 131:1; Isa 2:11; 3:16; Eze 28:2-5,9 Da 11:36,37; Hab 2:4; 2Th 2:3,4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-14","title":"Proverbs 30:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>whose. 12:18; Job 29:17; Ps 3:7; 52:2; 57:4; 58:6; Da 7:5-7; Re 9:8 to devour. 22:16; 28:3; Ps 10:8,9; 12:5; 14:4; Ec 4:1; Isa 32:7; Am 2:7; 4:1; 8:4 Mic 2:1,2; 3:1-5; Hab 3:14; Zep 3:3; Mt 23:14; Jas 5:1-4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-15","title":"Proverbs 30:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>The horseleach. Isa 57:3; Eze 16:44-46; Mt 23:32; Joh 8:39,44 Give. Isa 56:11,12; Ho 4:18; Mic 7:3; Ro 16:18; 2Pe 2:3,13-15 Jude 1:11,12 There. 21,24,29; 6:16; Am 1:3,6,9,11,13; 2:1,4 It is enough. Heb. Wealth.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-16","title":"Proverbs 30:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>27:20; Hab 2:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-17","title":"Proverbs 30:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>eye. 11; 20:20; 23:22; Ge 9:21-27; Le 20:9; De 21:18-21 2Sa 18:9,10,14-17 the ravens. 1Sa 17:44; 2Sa 21:10 valley. or, brook.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-18","title":"Proverbs 30:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>too. Job 42:3; Ps 139:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-19","title":"Proverbs 30:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>way of an. Job 39:27; Isa 40:31 midst. Heb. heart. and the. Ex 22:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-20","title":"Proverbs 30:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>7:13-23; Nu 5:11-30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-22","title":"Proverbs 30:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>a servant. 19:10; 28:3; Ec 10:7; Isa 3:4,5 a fool. 1Sa 25:3,10,11,25,36-38; 30:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-23","title":"Proverbs 30:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>an odious. 19:13; 21:9,19; 27:15 an handmaid. 29:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-24","title":"Proverbs 30:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>little. Job 12:7 exceeding wise. Heb. wise, made wise.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-25","title":"Proverbs 30:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>The ants may truly be called a people, as they have houses, towns, public roads, etc.; and shew their wisdom and prudence by preparing their meat in due season.</p>\n<p>6:6-8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-26","title":"Proverbs 30:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>Le 11:5; Ps 104:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-27","title":"Proverbs 30:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>The locusts. Ex 10:4-6,13-15; Ps 105:34; Joe 1:4,6,7; 2:7-11,25; Re 9:3-11 by bands. Heb. gathered together.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-30","title":"Proverbs 30:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>Nu 23:24; Jud 14:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-31","title":"Proverbs 30:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>greyhound. or, horse. Heb. girt in the lions. against. 16:14; 20:2; Da 3:15-18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-32","title":"Proverbs 30:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>thou hast done. 26:12; Ec 8:3 lay. 17:28; Job 21:5; 40:4; Ec 8:4; Mic 7:16,17; Ro 3:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-30-33","title":"Proverbs 30:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":30,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":30,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>so. 15:18; 16:28; 17:14; 26:21; 28:25; 29:22</p>"}]}